## Tests that are refused, and what replaces each one

The section is here and it says a great deal, and none of it is a line the
reader recognises. This is what a guide looks like after somebody reflows the
list into prose, and it is the shape that passes every other leg for free
because there is nothing left to judge.

A test that starts a desktop or GUI dependent server is refused, and so is one
that requires a GPU, and so is one that downloads a model.

## A later section

Here so the reader has something to stop at.
